  "sections": {
    "1": {
      "purpose": "This System Requirement Specification (SRS) defines the system-level requirements for the telemetry acquisition subsystem of the [Project Name] R&D project. This subsystem will support the [Parent System 1] and [Parent System 2] systems, providing real-time telemetry data acquisition and analysis capabilities.  The intended audience for this SRS is the development team, engineering staff, and stakeholders involved in the design, implementation, and testing of the telemetry acquisition system.\n\nThis document outlines the functional and non-functional requirements that must be met by the subsystem to ensure its successful integration with the parent systems and operation within the defined constraints.",
      "scope": "Scope\n\nThis System Requirement Specification (SRS) defines the system-level requirements for the Telemetry Acquisition Subsystem.\n\nIn Scope:\n\nThe acquisition and processing of telemetry data from at least three sensor channels simultaneously.\nTimestamping every acquired sample with a system time reference accurate to +/- 1 ms.\nBuffering acquired samples before flow control, with a minimum buffer size of 10,000 samples per channel.\nExposing acquired samples through a REST interface for ground segment access.\nRecording an engineering log with a minimum depth of six months of mission operations.\nEnsuring the system's operational reliability and availability (e.g., MTBF) as defined in REQ-0002, REQ-0007, REQ-0008, REQ-0009.\nPowering the system within a 28 V DC power envelope not exceeding 45 W.\n\nOut of Scope:\n\nDevelopment and implementation of specific sensor integration protocols or interfaces (e.g., specific communication protocols for each sensor).\nDetailed design of the telemetry acquisition hardware, including physical components and interfacing details.\nSpecific software development tasks beyond the core functionality defined in this SRS.\n\nNote: This document focuses on system-level requirements for the Telemetry Acquisition Subsystem. Further detailed specifications will be provided in subsequent documents.",
