    "2": {
      "system_context": "System Overview\n\nSystem Boundaries: This system is responsible for acquiring, timestamping, buffering, and transmitting telemetry data from multiple sensor channels to the ground segment via a REST interface. It operates within a defined power envelope of 28V DC with maximum power consumption of 45W.  The system's operation is constrained by a minimum depth of 6 months in its engineering log for mission operations.\n\nExternal Interfaces: The system interfaces with:\n\nSensor Channels: Acquires telemetry data from at least 3 sensor channels simultaneously.\nGround Segment: Exposes acquired samples through a REST interface to the ground segment.\nEngineering Log System: Records an engineering log with a minimum depth of 6 months for mission operations.\nPower Supply: Operates within a 28V DC power envelope not exceeding 45W.\n\nSystem Context: The system operates as part of a larger R&D project focused on developing advanced sensor technology and data analysis capabilities.  The system's functionality is essential for the project's success, enabling real-time data acquisition, processing, and transmission to support research and development activities.\n\nNotes:\n\nAll claims regarding system boundaries and external interfaces are grounded in the provided requirements document (SysRS_v3.1.docx).\nThe system operates within a defined power envelope of 28V DC with maximum power consumption of 45W. This is explicitly stated in the SysRS document.",
      "system_architecture": "System Overview: Architectural View\n\nThe system architecture consists of the following key components:\n\nSensor Interface:  Receives telemetry data from at least three sensor channels simultaneously.\nData Processing Unit (DPU): Processes and timestamps acquired samples with a reference to +/- 1 ms accuracy.\nBuffering Module: Provides buffering for at least 10,000 samples per channel before applying flow control.\nREST Interface: Exposes acquired samples through a REST interface for ground segment access.\nEngineering Log Module: Records an engineering log with a minimum depth of 6 months of mission operations.\nFault Recovery Unit:  Completes a software restart in less than 30 seconds after a fault.\n\nThe system operates within a 28 V DC power envelope not exceeding 45 W.\n\nNote: Detailed design information is provided in the System Design Document (SDD).",
